# Audio / DSP Conventions

- **Sample format is 32-bit fixed-point Q31** (`int32_t`), matching the
  existing `sine_table` and the `.ioc`'s `I2S_DATAFORMAT_32B` — not IEEE
  `float`/`double`. Every sample that reaches the DAC over I2S must be Q31.
  `double`/`float` are only acceptable in cold-path, one-time setup code
  (e.g. converting a typed-in frequency to a phase increment) — never in a
  per-sample generator or ISR/DMA callback. See `realtime-audio-performance.mdc`.
- **Never step a parameter instantaneously** if it's continuously read by
  DMA (gain, DC level, frequency) — slew-limit it like `DC_SLEW_STEP` in
  `audio_bridge.c` to avoid filter-ringing/output spikes.
- **Sample rate: 96 kHz is the current bring-up / boss-bench rate**
  (`AUDIO_SAMPLE_RATE_HZ` in `apps/channel_card/Core/Inc/audio/audio_rate.h`).
  Changing it requires lockstep: `.ioc` I2S1/I2S2 `AudioFreq`,
  `CS4304_SAMPLE_RATE_ACTIVE`, phase-increment denominators, and filter
  design `fs`. Never hardcode the rate in new generator code — always
  derive from `AUDIO_SAMPLE_RATE_HZ`.
- **DMA buffers touched by DMA1 must live in AXI SRAM** (the `.dma_buffer`
  linker section), never DTCM/`.bss` — DMA1 (D2 domain) cannot reach DTCM.
  See the buffer declarations and comment in `audio_bridge.c`.
- **Double-buffer discipline**: half/full DMA callbacks each own exactly one
  half of the buffer at a time — never write the half currently being read
  by the DMA engine.
- **Wavetable generation**: use a 32-bit fixed-point phase accumulator with
  linear interpolation between table entries (see `Tone_NextSineSample()`).
  Table size sets interpolation error, not the achievable frequency — the
  phase accumulator itself gives sub-mHz resolution at 96 kHz, more
  than enough for fractional-Hz tones.
